        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Yarra Yarra is a handsome detached coastal property with sea and harbour views, built in the 1890s by the La Touche family and is said to be one of three houses on Beach Road that have survived as a physical reminder of the late Victorian Greystones era.\n\nA particularly charming feature of Yarra Yarra is its enclosed entrance porch with its pitched tiled roof, delicate glazed panels and beautifully detailed timber fretwork complimenting the projecting Bay windows.\n\nOccupying three floors the property retains many of its original architectural features including high ceilings, ornate ceiling coving, original staircase and marble fireplaces whilst more recent improvements include the installation of double glazed sash windows, sympathetic to the character of the house, new radiators and a heat pump system. There is a grade C energy rating attached to the property.\n\nThe principal rooms are generously proportioned and retain a real sense of grandeur, a reflection of its historical back story with the more recent chapter as the base of the award winning telecommunications company Goldfish. With some simple reconfiguration its next chapter is more likely to become a family home in its entirety (subject to final approval by the WCC).\n\nThe existing accommodation provides the perfect framework for residential reinstatement as there are well proportioned reception rooms, a kitchen cum breakfast area, modern family shower room. At upper level, one of the property's most impressive spaces stretches the entire width of the house. Currently arranged as an open plan room, it captures spectacular views out towards the sea and harbour and could become an extraordinary principal bedroom suite, or open plan living space.\n\nThe front driveway is super wide providing parking for several cars as well as additional parking spots for a boat, trailer, or even a camper van. Not many properties within the Marina can offer up this space. To the rear there is an enclosed courtyard garden and a Mediterranean style roof top terrace.\n\nJust a five minute walk to Greystones main street the property is close to the towns train station, bus links, cafes, restaurants, speciality stores, pubs and boutiques as well as supermarkets and convenience stores. Beach, seafront and coastal walks are all within easy reach. It is a location that offers best of both worlds, the atmosphere and vibrancy of being part of a marina development together with the sense of privacy and individuality. \n\nAll in all Yara Yarra is a property with an historical background in a remarkable location representing both town and coastal living at its best.\n\nSPECIAL FEATURES\nEnviable location within walking distance of Greystones main street, Beach, Cove and Harbour.\nStunning sea, harbour and mountain views\nBer energy rating is grade C\nHeat pump Air to water heating system with heat pump.\nDouble glazed sash windows throughout entire house\nRecently installed radiators\nAttractive enclosed Victorian porch\nLeaded glass fan light and Victorian glass panels in hall door\nFeature projecting bay windows\nHigh ceilings with ornate ceiling coving.\nImpressive original staircase\nWell proportioned reception rooms with original internal doors. \nOriginal marble fireplaces throughout\nFully equipped kitchen cum dining area with side access.\nHigh specification fully tiled family shower room. Heated towel rail.\nGravelled driveway providing off street parking for several cars, boats and camper vans.\nOutdoor rear courtyard and mediterranean roof top terrace\nEntrance pillars and boundary wall to the front incorporating electronically controlled entrance gate.\n\nACCOMODATION\n\nEntrance Porch\nEnclosed porch with pitched tiled roof. Steps up to glass panelled door\nInternal hall door with glass panels and stained glass fan light. Cornicing both sides of door. \n\nEntrance hallway\nFeature Dado rails. High ceilings Original panelled doors lead into reception rooms. Lovely high ceilings and feature hardwood staircase. Attractive ceiling coving and architraves. \n\nDownstairs WC\nTiled floor. Wc and whb\n\nBedroom 4/Office\nFeature original marble fireplace with brass trim. Large sash window. Fitted wardrobes\n\nDrawing room\nFeature original marble fireplace with ornate inset tiles and cast iron grate. Picture rails and ceiling coving. Feature Bay window with three sash windows facing out towards the sea. Timber effect laminate flooring. Accessed via glass french doors:\n\nLiving room\nFitted cast iron stove with timber mantle. Fitted shelving. Door through to:\n\nKitchen cum dining area\nTiled floor and tiled splashbacks. Fitted high and low level fitted units with provision for dishwasher, fridge and oven. Fitted extractor hood and fan. Door to side. Fitted shelving. Storage cupboard.\n\nRear Lobby\nTiled floor. Boiler room. Understairs storage.\n\nPatio glass doors lead out to rear courtyard. Gravelled sheltered area ideal for al fresco dining. Composite fencing with concrete posts. Outdoor fitted electrical sockets\n\nUPSTAIRS\n\nLanding\nFeature stained glass fitted window. Fitted bookcases.\n\nInternal landing \nGlass door leads out to roof top terrace. Outdoor electrical sockets. Timber fencing with glass panels.\n\nFamily shower room \nDouble sized step in shower unit with glass screen with two shower connections featuring a large rose head connection. Fully tiled with stylish marble tiles. Heated towel rail. Ceramic whb set into vanity cabinet. Recessed lighting. Fitted wall mirror.\n\nBedroom 2\nFeature bay window. \n\nBedroom 3\nHigh ceilings\n\nTOP LANDING\nMaster Bedroom/Open plan room\nThis top sprawling open plan room spans the entire width of the house. This could be divided into two bedrooms, used as a master ensuite or open plan living space. Stunning views of the Irish Sea, Harbour and La Touche Hotel.\n\nOUTSIDE SPACES\nTo the Front\nSpacious gravelled driveway with lots of parking for different types of vehicles. Side boundary hedging and entrance walls and pillars incorporating electronically controlled entrance gate. \n\nTo the rear\nThe private courtyard garden is complemented by an impressive covered timber pergola, creating a wonderful sheltered outdoor room for dining and entertaining. The combination of warm timber, traditional white rendered walls and contemporary dark fencing creates an appealing contrast between the property's historic character and more modern additions.\n\nThe property also benefits from a superb private roof terrace, thoughtfully screened in natural timber and providing an exceptional outdoor entertaining space. Bathed in sunlight, it offers a wonderfully secluded setting for morning coffee or evening drinks, while enjoying an elevated outlook over the surrounding rooftops and out towards Bray Head."
